in @prism
in @mirror/cli
in @mirror/mosaic
in @mirror/pack
in @pack
in @peer
in @spectral/supervisor
in @song

# @mirror/spawn — the `mirror spawn ~peer'<home>'` cli-surface
# substrate-decl.
#
# Phase D close per the LOCAL-PACK loop. Lifts @pack.spawn (the
# load-bearing primitive at @pack altitude per recognition #84,
# shards/pack.mirror:273) to the cli surface where humans type
# `mirror spawn ~peer'~/.reed'` and get a running Reed.
#
# === What @mirror/spawn IS ===
#
# The cli-surface thin wrapper that:
#
#   1. Accepts a ~peer'<home>' argument (one positional arg)
#   2. Resolves it via @peer.load(dir, p) (672f434; G1-composed with
#      @io/git per Alex 2026-06-25 yes-confirmation)
#   3. Resolves contextual frame (current mirror.spec at @mirror/cli
#      altitude)
#   4. Resolves contextual repository (the resolved peer's home)
#   5. Resolves contextual pack (the current spec's pack{} block; see
#      mirror.spec dogfood 8107caf for the dogfood instance)
#   6. Discharges pack_coherent check (existing @pack bilateral)
#   7. Delegates to @pack.spawn with the resolved 5-tuple
#
# The substrate-pull point: at the cli surface a human says ONE thing
# (the target peer); the substrate resolves the rest from context. This
# is the substrate-vs-USE rule applied to invocation: USE specifies the
# target; substrate fills the context.
#
# === Phase H gate (the empirical proof) ===
#
# Phase H of the LOCAL-PACK loop: `mirror spawn ~peer'~/.reed'` returns
# running Reed via @fate (optical inference per recognition #58; NOT
# @io/llm). This shard makes that invocation TYPECHECK at substrate
# altitude; the actual Rust runtime + @fate composition lands at Alex's
# altitude (Phase G + H).
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - #84 (@pack multi-repo agent runtime; promoted): provides the
#   @pack.spawn primitive this shard wraps
# - #58 (Fate IS optical inference; promoted): @fate IS the inference
#   primitive; cascade/code/* species discharge the loop. NO @io/llm.
#   This shard does NOT declare `in @fate` because @fate is the
#   runtime substrate, not a substrate-decl prism (per Taut Phase F
#   anti-pattern correction 2026-06-24).
# - #99 (mirror.spec IS λ₀; Alex-named, Mara canonical d0b6519):
#   spawn at the cli surface is an EXCITATION above λ₀ — the substrate
#   moves out of ground state to produce a runtime peer. The spawn
#   action IS one of the spectral-gap-crossing operations.
# - peer-ACL spec §4 (lead semantics): the spawned peer at the spec's
#   root IS the lambda-shell counterparty; when `mirror spawn` runs
#   without an explicit target, the default IS the current spec's
#   pack{}.lead (forward-promised in this shard).
#
# === Composition with @spectral/supervisor (peer-ACL §2.4) ===
#
# Runtime lifecycle composition: @spectral/supervisor (existing glass
# at shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror:322) owns the spawned peer's
# lifecycle (restart_strategy, terminate). @mirror/spawn KICKS the
# spawn through @spectral/supervisor.start_child rather than directly
# instantiating; this preserves the lifecycle invariant for the
# spawned peer.
#
# Per peer-ACL §10 reframe: the lead is N+1 observer (spawn-and-probe
# relation, NOT delegation). @mirror/spawn discharges the SPAWN side;
# the spectral-Tomm-probe handling at runtime is the lead's ongoing
# responsibility.
#
# === Composition with @song/movement (Arc 6 close, 2026-07-06) ===
#
# `mirror spawn ~peer'<home>'` IS `@song/movement.enter(m, p)` at cli
# altitude — the frame-entry action of a temporal-bounded epoch at
# runtime. Per shards/song/movement.mirror §3 (`enter` — the movement's
# frame-open event): enter opens the bounded frame at species altitude,
# reads a movement's starting material (voices, progressions, phrases),
# and emits the frame-open cadence. When a human types the cli verb
# `mirror spawn`, they discharge exactly this frame-entry action: the
# spawned peer enters a bounded frame (movement altitude) whose closure
# ships settled crystals through StageFreight's five-stage cascade.
#
# The cli verb `mirror spawn` IS the species-altitude action `enter` at
# cli altitude. Same operation, two altitudes. The substrate-pull that
# closes this binding: cli-verbs ARE species-altitude actions.
#
# === Composition with @song/voice (peer as time-indexed trajectory) ===
#
# The spawned peer's runtime trajectory IS a `song_voice` — the agent's
# time-indexed trajectory through their authored sections (per
# shards/song/voice.mirror §Species positioning). The *when* on top of
# `@mirror/spectral/voice`'s *what/who*: @mirror/spectral/voice names
# the peer as actor at orchestra altitude; @song/voice adds the temporal
# dimension — that peer as actor at temporal altitude, unfolding a
# time-indexed trajectory through their spec.
#
# The spawn action births the song_voice. From the moment spawn returns,
# the spawned peer IS voicing their song — advancing through their
# spec's state space one moment at a time, discharging `voice_line_valid`
# at each cadence event.
#
# === Citations (M-cascade wiring) ===
#
# - Collapse spec `docs/specs/mcp-spec-song-collapse.md` §10 (Mara
#   `2cfd2a7`): the M-cascade wiring path names spawn's return type
#   upgrade as M2. Composes with #S2 (shift-at-temporal, LANDED),
#   #S3 (five-op temporal specialisation, LANDED), #S4 (cascade-shape
#   altitude-portable, LANDED). Per collapse spec §5.1: @song IS the
#   spec's time-evolution operator applied to a peer.
#
# - @spectral/gen_prism/mcp_session (M1 LANDED at `01443b3`): sibling
#   substrate. The MCP session gen_prism IS the state machine that
#   accumulates @spec across mq queries; @mirror/spawn IS the substrate
#   that consumes the ratified @spec into a running @song peer.
#   Together they close the mq → @spec → @song wiring: M1 accumulates
#   the spec, M2 spawns the peer whose trajectory IS the spec's time-
#   evolution.
#
# - #43 (mirror IS content-addressed build system; LANDED at M6 TICK 1
#   `884f433`; empirically substrate-fact per M1 TICK 1 `8eac1de` Seam
#   Phase D): spawn IS the second first-order consumer of the Apache-2.0
#   floor. The spawned peer's initial state IS an OID in @mirror/store;
#   the spawn action IS the CAS-advance from empty session ref to peer-
#   initialized ref. M6 store (floor) → M1 mcp_session (accumulator) →
#   M2 spawn (peer-launcher) forms the rock-solid stack.
#
# === Return-type upgrade (2026-07-06) ===
#
# Original 2026-06-25 landing returned opaque `runtime` — opaque because
# @song didn't exist yet; there was no typed temporal frame to name the
# spawned peer's trajectory. Arc 6 close (`eb50a61`) landed the @song
# family + 5 species (movement, voice, progression, narrative, phrase);
# this tick upgrades the return type from opaque `runtime` to typed
# `@song`. The spawned peer's temporal-progression trajectory IS a @song
# by structural specialization (not analogy):
#
# - identity: uuid_spectral (from @spectral/gen_prism)
# - state: shard_ref at the peer's evolving spec crystal
# - trajectory: song_progression (time-ordered path through spec state
#   space)
# - actions: song_voice (advance/settle), song_movement (enter/close)
#
# Taut's composition-points scout (post @song landing) flagged the
# 11-day-old type mismatch: spawn predates @song by 11 days (spawn
# 2026-06-25 vs @song 2026-07-06); its `runtime` return was a
# placeholder for a type that had not yet been declared. This tick
# closes the mismatch: the typed temporal frame now exists, so spawn
# returns @song at the family-root altitude. Species specialization
# (which of the 5 species applies at any given consumer altitude)
# happens at the consumer, not here.

prism @mirror/spawn {
  focus mirror_spawn_request
  project mirror_spawn_request
  split mirror_spawn_request
  shift mirror_spawn_request
  settle mirror_spawn_request
}

# === The mirror_spawn_request carrier ===
#
# The typed cli-surface request shape. Two fields:
#
#   target  — the peer to spawn (resolved via @peer.load from the
#             ~peer'<home>' cli argument). REQUIRED at cli altitude.
#
#   options — the spawn options (substrate-typed as `ref` until the
#             option-record carrier surfaces; current options include
#             --hello-world for the Phase H empirical proof gate,
#             --detach / --foreground, --restart-strategy override).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the (target, options) tuple.
type mirror_spawn_request = {
  target:  peer,
  options: ref,
}

# === spawn — the cli-surface action ===
#
# Lifts the cli invocation into the substrate. The contextual
# resolutions (frame, repository, pack) happen INSIDE the body via
# @mirror/cli's contextual lookup; the action signature surfaces only
# the request + perturbation.
#
# Returns @song per the return-type upgrade (see "Return-type upgrade"
# section above). The spawned peer's temporal-progression trajectory IS
# a @song — the peer's time-evolution operator applied to their spec.
# Composes with @spectral/supervisor for lifecycle (start_child kicks
# the spawn; restart_strategy owned by supervisor).
spawn(r: mirror_spawn_request, p: perturbation) -> @song
requires peer_well_known(r.target, p)
{ \ }

# === peer_well_known — sub-bilateral predicate ===
#
# Checks that r.target is a peer the substrate can actually spawn:
# the home repo exists (via @io/git.git_repository_open), the
# mirror.spec parses (via @mirror/spec), and a pack{}.lead resolves
# (via @peer.load + the self-naming rule per peer-ACL §6.2).
#
# Lifted to spawn's `requires` clause per recognition #53 family.
peer_well_known(p: peer, perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === Forward-promised — NOT landed this tick ===
#
# - default_target(spec_path: ref, p: perturbation) -> imperfect(peer, ref, ref)
#     When `mirror spawn` runs without explicit target, resolve to the
#     CURRENT spec's pack{}.lead. Closes the no-arg cli invocation.
#
# - mirror_spawn_coherent(r: mirror_spawn_request, p: perturbation) -> verdict
#     Composed bilateral per recognition #53 family (15th altitude lift
#     when it lands).

out @mirror/spawn
out mirror_spawn_request
out spawn
out peer_well_known
